From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] source-build: add the riscv64 OpenSSL target

ci/source-build/config.sh maps `uname -m` to the target name OpenSSL's
Configure expects and aborts on anything other than x86_64/aarch64, so
the from-source GDAL stack (and with it the Linux wheel) cannot be built
on riscv64 at all. OpenSSL has shipped a linux64-riscv64 target since
3.0; map riscv64 to it.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [one-line arch mapping, applies unchanged to upstream main]
---
 ci/source-build/config.sh | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ci/source-build/config.sh b/ci/source-build/config.sh
index 8cad992fe..98ad64a00 100644
--- a/ci/source-build/config.sh
+++ b/ci/source-build/config.sh
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ ARCH="$(uname -m)"
 case "${ARCH}" in
     x86_64)  OPENSSL_TARGET="linux-x86_64" ;;
     aarch64) OPENSSL_TARGET="linux-aarch64" ;;
+    riscv64) OPENSSL_TARGET="linux64-riscv64" ;;
     *) echo "ERROR: unsupported architecture ${ARCH}" >&2; exit 1 ;;
 esac

--
